## Maintenance
On any {{SYSTEM_NAME}} change: update the relevant `skills/*.md`, regenerate the manifest (or append a
`patches[]` entry for a mid-version fix), bump the version line in `CONTEXT.md` (and here) on a publish,
run the binding audit (zero unbound), then commit + push. Drift in the skills defeats the bootstrap.

## Agent orchestration (design-system agents)

This context is **design system only** — three role-based subagents. On any task, decide the moment in
the pipeline first, then delegate. Full map, pipeline, and operating rules: see `AGENTS-HANDOFF.md`.

| Route to | When | Write surface |
|---|---|---|
| `ds-steward` | tokens/styles, token architecture, governance, the binding-audit GATE, publish, drift, manifest, skills/docs, spiels mechanism, lookup | {{SYSTEM_NAME}} source variables/styles + the context repo |
| `component-designer` | build/modify components + variants/states/layout, bind to tokens | {{SYSTEM_NAME}} source component/component_set nodes |
| `brand-designer` | identity direction, illustration, photo/video, marketing creative | identity + expressive assets (DECISIONS handed to ds-steward) |
| _separate context_ | build consumer screens, flows/specs, coded prototypes | NOT handled here — `{{STUDIO_REPO}}` |

**The decide→encode→build→audit→publish pipeline:** `brand-designer` decides identity →
`ds-steward` encodes it as semantic tokens → `component-designer` builds + binds the components +
completes their states/a11y → `ds-steward` independently runs the binding-audit gate + the user clicks
Publish → updated skills/manifest hand off to the separate screen-creation context, which consumes the
published library. A gap found downstream routes back here as a tokenization request.

Operating rules (full detail in AGENTS-HANDOFF.md):
- Plan Mode is the gate before any source-variable/component write or publish — plan in `yaml`
  (type + name + bindings + honest gaps), approve, then build incrementally with render-verification.
- Load `skills/*.md` + `DESIGN.md` + the manifest fresh, never from memory.
- The binding audit is a publish GATE — zero unbound on any new/modified component. `clone()` does not
  carry bindings; re-bind after cloning.

Slash commands (thin wrappers that delegate to the agents — never duplicate the workflow, or it drifts):
`/design-system-check` (→ ds-steward) · `/binding-audit` (→ ds-steward) · `/drift-check` (→ ds-steward)
